From: slwyts <slwyts@foxmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] session-worker: close cancelled reauthentication requests

A reauthentication client cancels its old verifier before opening another
channel. Sending Reset back in response makes GNOME Shell 51 restart that
sequence, repeatedly cancelling and reopening authentication before the
password prompt can be used. Stop its conversations without sending a
reset notification; the client is already cancelling or restarting them.

Close the session before dropping a replaced or disconnected request.
Conversations retain their session, so unref alone leaves a pending PAM
worker and its D-Bus connections alive until it exits. Repeated requests
can exhaust the login worker's file descriptors and prevent unlocking.
---
--- a/daemon/gdm-session-worker.c
+++ b/daemon/gdm-session-worker.c
@@ -3098,7 +3098,7 @@ on_reauthentication_cancelled (GdmSession              *session,
                                ReauthenticationRequest *request)
 {
         g_debug ("GdmSessionWorker: client cancelled reauthentication request");
-        gdm_session_reset (session);
+        gdm_session_close (session);
 }
 
 static void
@@ -3354,6 +3354,7 @@ reauthentication_request_free (ReauthenticationRequest *request)
         g_signal_handlers_disconnect_by_func (request->session,
                                               G_CALLBACK (on_reauthentication_verification_complete),
                                               request);
+        gdm_session_close (request->session);
         g_clear_object (&request->session);
         g_slice_free (ReauthenticationRequest, request);
 }
